# Branch policy

**Full doc:** [.github/BRANCH_POLICY.md](../../.github/BRANCH_POLICY.md)

## Required format

```
{action}/{user}/{description}
```

| Segment | Values |
|---------|--------|
| **action** | `feat`, `fix`, `doc`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `spec`, `hotfix` |
| **user** | GitHub login or tool name — e.g. `ritz-ras1245`, `cursor`, `dependabot` |
| **description** | kebab-case slug |

**Examples:** `feat/cursor/p49-docker-spike`, `doc/cursor/cloud-setup`, `fix/cursor/session-end-clear`

**Exception:** `release/N.x` only (RVS patch lines).

## Rules

- **Never commit on `main`** — work on a named branch; merge to `main` only
- **Cloud / bot agents:** open a **PR** — do not merge to `main`
- **Local agents:** before `git checkout -b`, use `{action}/cursor/{description}` (or `ritz-ras1245` when acting as owner)

## Cursor Cloud Agents — branch prefix (required)

Cloud Agents create the branch **before** this rule runs. Repo rules cannot override the platform prefix.

Set **Branch prefix** once in Cursor:

1. **Cursor Settings → Cloud Agents → Branch prefix**, or
2. [Cloud Agents dashboard → My defaults](https://cursor.com/dashboard/cloud-agents#my-defaults)

Use **`feat/cursor`** (no trailing slash). Cursor appends `/` + a slug → e.g. `feat/cursor/p49-docker-spike`, which passes CI.

| Work type | Prefix to use | Example result |
|-----------|---------------|----------------|
| Features (default) | `feat/cursor` | `feat/cursor/add-health-endpoint` |
| Docs only | `doc/cursor` | `doc/cursor/update-agents-md` |
| Fixes | `fix/cursor` | `fix/cursor/session-end-clear` |

Change the prefix in dashboard before starting a doc/fix Cloud Agent if you need the correct `action` segment.

**Alternative:** start the agent on an existing compliant branch (API: `workOnCurrentBranch: true` + `startingRef`).
